WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.840
This is a tour of the operator controls of the Cat 320D excavator, taken from its Operation and Maintenance Manual.

00:00:08.840 --> 00:00:17.800
Here is the cab from above. Each control has a number in the manual. Pause at any time and ask Cat about what you see.

00:00:17.800 --> 00:00:24.850
The heater and air-conditioner keep the operator comfortable in both hot and cold conditions.

00:00:24.850 --> 00:00:32.300
The heater and air-conditioner keep the operator comfortable while working in a range of temperature conditions.

00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:45.630
The hydraulic lockout lever sits on the left side of the left console; pulling it back locks all factory-installed hydraulic controls, while pushing it forward unlocks them for operation.

00:00:45.630 --> 00:00:57.280
When traveling, keep the final drive sprockets beneath the rear of the machine; releasing the travel levers or pedals returns them to center and applies the travel brakes.

00:00:57.280 --> 00:01:03.760
Move both travel levers or pedals equally in the same direction to travel straight.

00:01:03.760 --> 00:01:12.530
This display shows the total operating hours of the engine. Use it to work out the service hour maintenance intervals.

00:01:12.530 --> 00:01:23.140
The monitor displays various operating information about the machine. The Monitoring System section of the manual explains how to use it.

00:01:23.140 --> 00:01:33.430
The joystick control operates the work-tool functions, with detailed individual joystick functions described elsewhere in the manual.

00:01:33.430 --> 00:01:44.920
Turn the engine speed dial clockwise to increase rpm or counter-clockwise to decrease it, with the selected position shown on the electronic monitor panel.

00:01:44.920 --> 00:01:57.370
Turn the key clockwise to ON to activate all cab circuits, and on to START to crank the engine. Release the key after the engine starts. Turn it to OFF to stop the engine.

00:01:57.370 --> 00:02:05.140
The operator's seat and console provide multiple adjustments to suit a wide range of operators.

00:02:05.140 --> 00:02:13.070
The 320D can be equipped with a radio; details are covered in the manual’s Radio section.

00:02:13.070 --> 00:02:25.400
The backup switches are under the right armrest. With switch 12A in MANUAL, the electronic controller is disconnected and the monitor shows LIMITED MOBILITY MODE.

00:02:25.400 --> 00:02:35.400
When backup switch 12A stays in the AUTOMATIC position, the electronic controller governs engine speed and the backup switches are inactive.

00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:40.960
Now the right side control panel, with switches 13 to 26.

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:52.970
Press it to choose LOW SPEED for rough or soft ground or loading onto a trailer, or AUTOMATIC for fast travel on hard, level ground. Don't change it while you travel.

00:02:52.970 --> 00:03:07.980
The Automatic Engine Speed Control reduces engine speed when the machine is idle, helping lower fuel use, noise, and wear, and returns to the dial setting whenever a hydraulic function is activated.

00:03:07.980 --> 00:03:14.990
Press the Travel Alarm Cancel Switch to stop the alarm, and the indicator lamp will illuminate.

00:03:14.990 --> 00:03:24.160
Press the Work Tool Control switch to show the selected tool on the monitor, and press it repeatedly to cycle through the available tools.

00:03:24.160 --> 00:03:36.210
Press the button to activate heavy lift mode, which raises hydraulic relief pressure for greater lifting force and slows cylinder speed; press again to deactivate the mode.

00:03:36.210 --> 00:03:47.980
Push the window washer switch; the indicator lights, washer fluid sprays from the nozzle, and the wiper runs while held, stopping about three seconds after release.

00:03:47.980 --> 00:03:59.470
Press the window wiper switch once for a six-second intermittent wipe, twice for three-second intervals, three times for continuous wipe, and four times to turn it off.

00:03:59.470 --> 00:04:10.960
Press the light switch once to activate Pattern 1, lighting the chassis work light D and cab lights F; press it twice for Pattern 2, adding boom light E.

00:04:10.960 --> 00:04:16.400
When both indicator lights are off, all of the work lights are turned off.

00:04:16.400 --> 00:04:25.610
Moving the switch to LOCK engages the quick coupler with the work tool, while moving it to UNLOCKED disengages the coupler and triggers an alarm.

00:04:25.610 --> 00:04:35.180
Push down the top of switch (22) to turn the lower window wiper on, and push down the bottom portion of the switch to turn it off.

00:04:35.180 --> 00:04:49.030
Press the top of the switch and hold it down to activate the lower window washer, causing fluid to spray from the nozzle; continuous operation beyond twenty seconds may cause motor failure.

00:04:49.030 --> 00:05:02.560
In cold weather, press the top of the seat-heater switch to turn it on, and push the bottom to turn it off; the thermostat disables the heater when cabin temperature exceeds 10 °C.

00:05:02.560 --> 00:05:15.490
Fine swing delays the swing parking brake for 6.5 seconds after the swing joystick returns to neutral, so the swing drifts instead of stopping abruptly. Turn it off on a slope.

00:05:15.490 --> 00:05:27.700
When lifting, it sounds a buzzer if the load is unstable; then reduce the bucket load or move the stick inward. Push the right side of the switch to turn it on.

00:05:27.700 --> 00:05:31.500
Push the left side of the switch to turn it off.

00:05:31.500 --> 00:05:36.380
Pause this video at any control and ask Cat what it does.
